      "title": "Lethal trifecta (TC1): public issue content can induce reads from private repositories and exfiltrate through a public pull request",
      "horizon": "present",
      "finding_kind": "path",
      "attack_path": [
        {
          "ref": "in.public_issue",
          "note": "Untrusted issue content can enter the agent context when reviewing open issues in the public repo."
        },
        {
          "ref": "cap.read_private_repo",
          "note": "The MCP server exposes private repo reads using the user's personal token with repo scope across all owned repositories."
        },
        {
          "ref": "cap.create_pr_public",
          "note": "The agent can create a pull request on the public repo, which is attacker-readable egress."
        }
